  "description": "DAVZOR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H96 N8 Nd6 O28 2+,2(Cl1 1-),4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd3A (Nd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.610-4.001 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.60-112.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd6(L1)4(OH)4(MeOH)4]·2Cl·4MeOH (C84H112N8O32Cl2Nd6; L1 = deprotonated N,N'-bis(3-methoxysalicylidene)(propylene-2-ol)-1,3-diamine). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
